---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Graph node for the consultancy. ProfessionalService gives Google the
// service-business chip; Organization gives it the entity (logo, sameAs,
// founder) so the knowledge panel can disambiguate; WebSite anchors the
// site identity so AI assistants can connect citation chunks back to the
// canonical entity. Sitelinks SearchAction is intentionally omitted:
// Google retired the sitelinks search box from SERPs on 2024-11-21, so
// it produces no rich result. The three nodes are merged into a single
// @graph response so crawlers consume them together.
const homepageGraph = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "@id": "https://codyasmith.com/#organization",
      "name": "Cody Smith",
      "url": "https://codyasmith.com",
      "logo": {
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        "url": "https://codyasmith.com/icon-512.png",
        "width": 512,
        "height": 512
      },
      "founder": { "@id": "https://codyasmith.com/about#person" },
      "email": "cody@codyasmith.com",
      "telephone": "+1-435-868-7133",
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        "addressLocality": "Cedar City",
        "addressRegion": "UT",
        "addressCountry": "US"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ProfessionalService",
      "@id": "https://codyasmith.com/#service",
      "name": "Cody Smith",
      "url": "https://codyasmith.com",
      "description": "Web management, strategy consulting, implementation, and training for businesses that have outgrown their website.",
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        "addressLocality": "Cedar City",
        "addressRegion": "UT",
        "addressCountry": "US"
      },
      "email": "cody@codyasmith.com",
      "telephone": "+1-435-868-7133",
      "serviceType": ["Web Management", "Strategy Consulting", "Implementation", "Training"],
      "areaServed": { "@type": "Country", "name": "United States" }
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "@id": "https://codyasmith.com/#website",
      "url": "https://codyasmith.com",
      "name": "Cody Smith",
      "description": "Web management, strategy consulting, implementation, and training for businesses in Cedar City, Utah and beyond.",
      "publisher": { "@id": "https://codyasmith.com/#organization" },
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
    }
  ]
});
---

<Base title="Cody Smith | Web Management & Strategy Consulting in Cedar City, UT">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={homepageGraph} />

  {/* ============================================
       MASTHEAD
       Asymmetric broadsheet opening. Dateline at
       the top, hairline rule, dramatic h1 with the
       italic "a while ago." pulled into its own
       optical-axis treatment. No card, no eyebrow.
       ============================================ */}
  <section class="broadsheet pt-ed-7 pb-ed-6">
    <div class="reveal" style="--i:0">
      <p class="dateline">
        <span>No. 01</span>
        <span class="dateline-divider"></span>
        <span>Cedar City, Utah</span>
        <span class="dateline-divider"></span>
        <span>Established by hand</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="masthead-rule-thick reveal mt-ed-3" style="--i:0" />

    <h1 class="display-h1 reveal mt-ed-5" style="--i:1">
      <span data-personalize="hero-name" style="display:none"></span>Your business outgrew<br />
      its website <em>a while ago.</em>
    </h1>

    <hr class="masthead-rule-hair mt-ed-5" />

    <div class="editorial-grid mt-ed-5">
      <aside class="reveal pt-ed-2" style="--i:2">
        <p class="byline">Filed under</p>
        <p class="byline mt-ed-1" style="color: var(--color-neutral-300); letter-spacing: 0.14em">
          Consulting · Web · Marketing
        </p>
        <p class="byline mt-ed-4">Issue</p>
        <p class="byline mt-ed-1" style="color: var(--color-neutral-300); letter-spacing: 0.14em">
          Vol. 01
        </p>
      </aside>

      <div>
        <p class="lede reveal" style="--i:2" data-vibe="default">
          You know it. You've known it for a while. The site hasn't been touched in months. The analytics might be good or bad but nobody can tell you which. The developer who built the thing stopped returning emails. And every week you think "I need to do something about the website" and then something more urgent lands on your desk and you don't.
        </p>
        <p class="lede reveal" style="--i:2;display:none" data-vibe="beach">
          You've built something people are finding. Traffic is up, referrals are growing, the reputation is real. But the website doesn't reflect any of that. It looks like a business half the size you actually are. The world is starting to pay attention and your front door still looks like 2019.
        </p>
        <p class="lede reveal" style="--i:2;display:none" data-vibe="mountain">
          The business is already working but the infrastructure under it isn't ready for what comes next. The hosting is someone else's problem. The analytics are somebody's guess. The last developer left and took the passwords with them. Meanwhile you're growing on top of a foundation you can't see and can't control.
        </p>

        <div class="reveal flex flex-wrap items-center gap-ed-5 mt-ed-5" style="--i:3">
          <a href="/services" class="cta-stamp">
            See how I work
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/contact" class="cta-link">or just get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ============================================
       SECTION 01: THE WORK
       Typographic service list with a sticky
       section marker on the left. Each row is a
       hairline-separated typographic entry with
       a numeric column, a display-serif heading,
       a body paragraph, and an italic arrow. No
       cards.
       ============================================ */}
  <section class="broadsheet pt-ed-6 pb-ed-6">
    <div class="editorial-grid">
      <aside class="section-marker reveal" style="--i:0">
        <span class="section-marker__num">01</span>
        <span class="section-marker__label">The work</span>
      </aside>

      <div>
        <h2 class="display-h2 reveal" style="--i:1" data-vibe="default">
          I close the gap between the business you've built and the website representing it.
        </h2>
        <h2 class="display-h2 reveal" style="--i:1;display:none" aria-hidden="true" data-vibe="beach">
          I help businesses look as good online as they actually are.
        </h2>
        <h2 class="display-h2 reveal" style="--i:1;display:none" aria-hidden="true" data-vibe="mountain">
          I make sure the infrastructure under your business is as solid as the business itself.
        </h2>

        <ol class="service-ol reveal-stagger mt-ed-5">
          <li class="reveal" style="--i:0">
            <a href="/services/web-management">
              <span class="service-ol__num">01</span>
              <span class="service-ol__name">Web Management</span>
              <span class="service-ol__arrow" aria-hidden="true">⤳</span>
              <p class="service-ol__body" data-phase="default">
                Most of my clients don't know who hosts their website. The SSL expired two months ago and a customer mentioned the warning screen before anyone on staff noticed. I take over the infrastructure, keep it alive, and send you proof every month that it's handled.
              </p>
              <p class="service-ol__body" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">
                Your website should be the one thing you never worry about. I take over the hosting, security, updates, and monitoring so you can focus on the business itself. One less thing on your plate. Every month you get proof it's handled.
              </p>
              <p class="service-ol__body" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">
                Dedicated cloud hosting, daily backups, SSL management, uptime monitoring, core and plugin updates. Monthly plain-language reports showing exactly what happened. I take over the infrastructure so you stop finding out something broke from a customer.
              </p>
            </a>
          </li>

          <li class="reveal" style="--i:1">
            <a href="/services/marketing-strategy">
              <span class="service-ol__num">02</span>
              <span class="service-ol__name">Strategy Consulting</span>
              <span class="service-ol__arrow" aria-hidden="true">⤳</span>
              <p class="service-ol__body" data-phase="default">
                You've got twelve opinions about what the business should do next and no outside read on which ones matter. I bring a marketing-fluent eye to visibility, positioning, search, operations, vendors, hiring, and growth decisions. Advice only. I help you see the move.
              </p>
              <p class="service-ol__body" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">
                Your business needs direction before it needs more tactics. I look at where you are, where the market is moving, and what decision needs to happen next. You'll know what to do first and why it matters. Advice only.
              </p>
              <p class="service-ol__body" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">
                Competitive analysis, search and content strategy, brand positioning, operations questions, vendor reads, hiring guidance. I sort through the noise, name the priorities with data behind them, and tell you what to do first. Consulting does not execute.
              </p>
            </a>
          </li>

          <li class="reveal" style="--i:2">
            <a href="/services/implementation">
              <span class="service-ol__num">03</span>
              <span class="service-ol__name">Implementation</span>
              <span class="service-ol__arrow" aria-hidden="true">⤳</span>
              <p class="service-ol__body">
                When the answer is a page, integration, analytics setup, feature, or build, it gets scoped as implementation. Written scope first. Fixed project shape before work starts. No vague bucket of "we'll figure it out later."
              </p>
            </a>
          </li>

          <li class="reveal" style="--i:3">
            <a href="/services/training">
              <span class="service-ol__num">04</span>
              <span class="service-ol__name">Training</span>
              <span class="service-ol__arrow" aria-hidden="true">⤳</span>
              <p class="service-ol__body">
                Your team sat through a webinar last year. Two hours of someone sharing their screen and saying "any questions?" three times. A week later nobody remembered how to add a blog post. I build guided programs where people learn by doing real work on their own systems, not by watching someone else do it.
              </p>
            </a>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ============================================
       SECTION 02: THE COLUMNIST
       Editorial profile. Drop cap on the opening
       paragraph, two body paragraphs in the reading
       face, then the pull-quote moment.
       ============================================ */}
  <section class="broadsheet pt-ed-6 pb-ed-6">
    <div class="editorial-grid">
      <aside class="section-marker reveal" style="--i:0">
        <span class="section-marker__num">02</span>
        <span class="section-marker__label">How I got here</span>
      </aside>

      <div>
        <p class="body-news-large reveal" style="--i:1">
          I got hired as a staff writer at a small newspaper in southern Utah. Within a year I was running their entire digital presence. The same thing happened at every job after that. Copywriting gig turned into a training program for 50,000 teachers. Creative director role turned into analytics and data strategy. "Marketing Representative" at a fiber co-op turned into running strategy, web development, and brand architecture for 30,500 members across two states.
        </p>

        <p class="body-news-large mt-ed-4 reveal" style="--i:2">
          The titles never described the work. The work was always the same: walk into a room, find the three things nobody's handling, handle them.
        </p>

        <div class="reveal mt-ed-6" style="--i:3">
          <p class="pull-quote">Now I do it on purpose.</p>
        </div>

        <a href="/about" class="cta-link reveal inline-flex items-baseline gap-ed-2 mt-ed-5" style="--i:4">
          Read the longer version
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ============================================
       SECTION 03: TEAR-OUT COUPON
       The free tool, framed like a torn-out page
       coupon. Dashed border, rotated 0.6deg, FREE
       COUPON tab on the upper edge. Hover
       straightens the block and warms the border.
       ============================================ */}
  <section class="broadsheet pt-ed-6 pb-ed-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto reveal" style="--i:0">
      <div class="coupon">
        <p class="byline">Compliments of the house</p>
        <h3 class="display-h2 mt-ed-3" style="font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.2vw, 2.625rem);">
          What does the internet think of your business?
        </h3>

        <p class="body-news mt-ed-3" data-processing="default">
          Type in your business name. I'll pull every mention I can find, read the sentiment, and show you what people are actually saying. Free. No login. No pitch afterward.
        </p>
        <p class="body-news mt-ed-3" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">
          Enter your brand name and get a scored sentiment report. Reviews, forums, news mentions, social. All pulled from across the web, analyzed, and scored 0 to 100. Free. No login. No pitch afterward.
        </p>
        <p class="body-news mt-ed-3" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">
          Ever wonder what people say about your business when you're not in the room? Type in your name and find out. I'll read every mention I can find and tell you the story the internet is telling about you. Free. No strings.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-ed-4 flex items-baseline justify-between">
          <a href="/listener" class="cta-link">Run the scanner →</a>
          <span class="folio-num" style="color: var(--color-amber-400)">Redeemable anytime</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ============================================
       SECTION 04: CLOSING STAMP
       The closing CTA. Large display headline,
       single-line body, postmark-style stamp button.
       ============================================ */}
  <section class="broadsheet pt-ed-6 pb-ed-8">
    <hr class="masthead-rule" />

    <div class="mt-ed-6 reveal" style="--i:0">
      <p class="byline">Closing notice</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="display-h1 reveal mt-ed-3" style="--i:1; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6.5vw, 5.5rem);" data-personalize="first-visit">
      Sound familiar<span data-personalize="name-comma" style="display:none"></span>?
    </h2>
    <h2 class="display-h1 reveal mt-ed-3" style="--i:1; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6.5vw, 5.5rem); display:none;" data-personalize="returning">
      Still thinking about it<span data-personalize="name-comma" style="display:none"></span>?
    </h2>

    <div class="editorial-grid mt-ed-5">
      <aside class="reveal" style="--i:2">
        <p class="byline">Postage</p>
        <p class="byline mt-ed-1" style="color: var(--color-neutral-300); letter-spacing: 0.14em">
          Reply within<br />one business day
        </p>
      </aside>

      <div>
        <p class="lede reveal" style="--i:2" data-personalize="first-visit" data-frame="default">
          If you read three of those and thought "that's us," we should probably talk. No pitch deck. No discovery call theater. Just tell me what's going on.
        </p>
        <p class="lede reveal" style="--i:2;display:none" data-personalize="first-visit" data-frame="sun">
          You've got the business. Let's get you the website it deserves. No pitch deck. No discovery call theater. Just a conversation about where you're headed.
        </p>
        <p class="lede reveal" style="--i:2;display:none" data-personalize="first-visit" data-frame="moon">
          If you read three of those and thought "that's us," we should probably talk. No pitch deck. No discovery call theater. Just tell me what's broken and I'll tell you what I'd do about it.
        </p>
        <p class="lede reveal" style="--i:2;display:none" data-personalize="returning">
          No pressure. But the website isn't fixing itself. Whenever you're ready, I'm here.
        </p>

        <div class="reveal mt-ed-5" style="--i:3">
          <a href="/contact" class="cta-stamp">
            Start a conversation
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
